    "result_text": "The full acceptance suite (Cp01\u2013Cp19) is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily create-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100+ owners already carry today's `registrationDate`.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (and mirroring the existing `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`/`CityAtCapacity...` city-capacity rule), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 counts stored owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws the checked `DailyOwnerLimitException` at `DAILY_LIMIT = 100`. Runs before `SaveOwner` so the request itself isn't counted.\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 checked exception carrying the current count.\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitHandler`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 maps it to a 429 `ProblemDetail` response, using the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper.\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `...DailyOwnerLimitException.yml` wiring the exception to the handler.\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted a `checkDailyLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `checkCityCapacity` and `build`, with `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp19Tests` (create 100 today \u2192 101st rejected with 429) now passes, and Cp18 (city capacity, 409) plus the rest of the suite remain green \u2014 confirming no regressions.",
